1
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:06,670
You scared me half to death.

2
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:09,130
I'm sorry. / It's okay. It's totally fine.

3
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:10,900
When Star fell in the water,

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,800
all I could do was shout. I couldn't actually help him at all.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,600
But I think it was your shouting, Time,

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,130
that told everyone Star fell in.

7
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:20,130
Physics has made it so damn obvious he's liked you since M.2.

8
00:00:20,130 --> 00:00:20,970
M.2?

9
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:22,900
Never lose power? Light a candle, Fuen.

10
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:24,270
Why'd you buy me candles?

11
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:25,230
In case of a blackout.

12
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,370
How did you stand it?

13
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:27,630
Because I like you so much.

14
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:30,100
I'm scared that if I cross that line,

15
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:31,830
and I lose the best friend I have in you,

16
00:00:31,830 --> 00:00:33,000
I couldn't take it.

17
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,030
At this year's event,

18
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:34,970
watch fireworks with me.

19
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:37,030
I'd like to get your contact, Din.

20
00:00:37,030 --> 00:00:38,200
I think you should go home.

21
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:39,500
You may be my idol,

22
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:40,970
but I have to protect my friend.

23
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:42,330
I don't want Chemi to misread me.

24
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:43,930
I already told Fuen how I feel.

25
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:45,900
I guess time will tell.

26
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:49,730
If two people are meant to be, they'll always find each other.

27
00:00:49,730 --> 00:00:53,130
Your life's been quite the mess lately.

28
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:54,270
I'm sorry, Star.

29
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:56,170
I can't help you win over Physics anymore.

30
00:00:56,170 --> 00:00:57,170
That camera.

31
00:00:57,170 --> 00:00:58,470
Can I buy it from you?

32
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:01,270
So I bought it off Star. This camera is mine now.

33
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,770
Please take it.

34
00:01:02,770 --> 00:01:05,600
Anything you buy for me on purpose, I want all of it.

35
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,230
Your heart is pounding right now.

36
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:08,230
I like it.

37
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:06,300
Everyone, turn to page 38.

38
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:20,230
Excuse me, teacher.

39
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:22,829
Council business with the juniors today?

40
00:03:22,829 --> 00:03:23,930
It's something important.

41
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:26,329
So could I borrow a moment of your time?

42
00:03:26,329 --> 00:03:27,500
Sure, sure, go ahead.

43
00:03:34,430 --> 00:03:35,630
Hey, juniors.

44
00:03:37,130 --> 00:03:39,430
Could I get Star's contact?

45
00:03:42,329 --> 00:03:43,470
No!

46
00:03:46,730 --> 00:03:48,170
Looks like you've forgotten,

47
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:51,329
that Star is the pride of Class King.

48
00:03:51,329 --> 00:03:55,270
So our class has rules for getting Star's contact.

49
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,070
My contact doesn't come that easy, Din.

50
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:06,200
Maybe I really did forget. So what are they?

51
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:18,670
"Mission: Rules for Getting Star's LINE"

52
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:24,030
If you want the LINE ID of Class King's pride,

53
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:26,070
you have to pass the missions.

54
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:31,030
But if you don't want to do them, there's another option.

55
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:34,800
And what's that?

56
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:37,230
There are 20 IDs in total.

57
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:40,100
Special price for you: 3,000 baht each.

58
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:44,970
Is this for real?

59
00:04:44,970 --> 00:04:46,530
It is.

60
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:53,030
So... if I want 20 LINE IDs,

61
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:57,730
I just have to pass 20 missions, right?

62
00:04:57,730 --> 00:04:59,000
Yes.

63
00:05:08,670 --> 00:05:09,970
Deal.

64
00:05:10,970 --> 00:05:13,770
When the missions start, have Time message me.

65
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:21,570
Hard or easy, don't worry.

66
00:05:21,570 --> 00:05:24,070
Because I'm sure I'll pass every single one.

67
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:42,000
Thank you, teacher.

68
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,370
Right! Can we get on with class now?

69
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:39,070
Chok, you lost. Buy us all a meal.

70
00:06:39,070 --> 00:06:41,800
Fine. Where do you guys want to eat? Pick one.

71
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,200
Too lazy to think. I'm beat.

72
00:06:46,530 --> 00:06:47,370
Din.

73
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:50,030
Can I ask you something?

74
00:06:50,730 --> 00:06:51,470
What?

75
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,900
Why'd you agree to do the missions?

76
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,900
You guys told me to go ask, so I went.

77
00:06:58,330 --> 00:06:59,970
And the juniors gave me missions to do.

78
00:06:59,970 --> 00:07:00,970
So I have to do them.

79
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,070
But from what I've heard,

80
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:06,200
whoever does Star's missions is someone who likes Star.

81
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:08,930
Just tell him you need his contact for work.

82
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,000
Mm-hmm.

83
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:14,170
Din.

84
00:07:15,670 --> 00:07:17,670
Or do you like Star?

85
00:07:18,770 --> 00:07:20,130
What's with you guys?

86
00:07:23,870 --> 00:07:25,770
I think it's kind of fun.

87
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:27,200
Don't you guys think so?

88
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:30,530
I think it's more than just fun.

89
00:07:30,530 --> 00:07:32,430
Are you smitten with Star or what?

90
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,230
Or did he spark joy?

91
00:07:35,670 --> 00:07:36,870
When you carried him out?

92
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:37,670
Mm.

93
00:07:37,670 --> 00:07:38,600
What's wrong with you?

94
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,370
Listen up, guys.

95
00:07:48,370 --> 00:07:51,270
If I had to choose between doing missions and paying 60,000 baht,

96
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:53,200
obviously I'd pick the first option, right?

97
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:55,970
You guys are imagining total nonsense.

98
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,700
Nonsense or not...

99
00:07:59,670 --> 00:08:01,430
Just don't let me find out

100
00:08:02,570 --> 00:08:03,700
that you...

101
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:06,770
that you...

102
00:08:14,530 --> 00:08:16,030
Are you going to keep chatting?

103
00:08:17,170 --> 00:08:20,830
This is class time. Go on, back to studying!

104
00:08:20,830 --> 00:08:21,900
Sorry, teacher.

105
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:27,770
Can I leave the juniors with you for a bit?

106
00:08:27,770 --> 00:08:28,530
Sure.

107
00:08:30,930 --> 00:08:32,030
Half an hour, okay?

108
00:08:32,630 --> 00:08:33,770
Yes, teacher.

109
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:08,300
"What are you thinking about? Din?"

110
00:09:21,570 --> 00:09:24,900
"Hmm, just a little curious. I don't get why he agreed to it."

111
00:09:30,870 --> 00:09:34,600
"Don't overthink it. You'll find out soon enough."

112
00:10:03,430 --> 00:10:08,000
"Let's start the first mission this evening. Any suggestions?"

113
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,400
"Start easy. Either treat him to a meal or walk him home."

114
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:14,570
"Easy my ass. Walk him home? Just carry his bag first."

115
00:10:14,570 --> 00:10:16,470
"Tough. Star won't go for it."

116
00:10:16,470 --> 00:10:18,630
"Yeah, Star won't go for it."

117
00:10:18,630 --> 00:10:19,730
"Daaamn, I think it works."

118
00:10:28,370 --> 00:10:29,370
"So the first mission is"

119
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:33,100
"take Star to his tutoring class."

120
00:10:37,230 --> 00:10:38,970
Hey! What are you all doing?

121
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,300
Don't let me catch any of you on your phones!

122
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:07,370
Hey, could I get a cold towel?

123
00:11:07,370 --> 00:11:08,300
Sure.

124
00:11:14,130 --> 00:11:15,900
Thanks. / Here you go.

125
00:11:16,270 --> 00:11:17,730
Oh, Chemi. / Yes?

126
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:21,570
FUN VIBE and I have a gig at the school event.

127
00:11:21,570 --> 00:11:23,630
Would you be interested in joining the band?

128
00:11:24,230 --> 00:11:25,430
Could I?

129
00:11:25,430 --> 00:11:29,000
Of course. Since that day at Siam,

130
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:31,970
I've felt we play really well together.

131
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:35,070
Phrues and Ply still talk about you to this day.

132
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:37,000
Really? / Yeah.

133
00:11:37,330 --> 00:11:40,130
Go for it. You can totally do it.

134
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:43,200
Interested?

135
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:47,700
Then I'll give it a try.

136
00:11:49,330 --> 00:11:52,800
But if I'm causing any problems, just tell me straight.

137
00:11:54,170 --> 00:11:57,730
Great. So whenever we have practice, I'll message you.

138
00:11:57,730 --> 00:11:58,500
Okay.

139
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:00,570
Let's exchange contacts.

140
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:02,600
Sure.

141
00:12:11,130 --> 00:12:12,400
Here. Okay.

142
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,370
Thanks. / See you.

143
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:22,100
Yes, sir.

144
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:22,900
Let's start.

145
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:24,730
Come on, let's practice.

146
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,100
Hurry, get up, get up.

147
00:12:29,670 --> 00:12:32,530
Aof! / Yes, Coach.

148
00:12:33,130 --> 00:12:34,370
Get the ball, go!

149
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:39,630
Play fair, okay?

150
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:50,800
Hey, why's Aof playing like that?

151
00:12:58,530 --> 00:13:00,800
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

152
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,300
He took it. I've got to get it back.

153
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:08,730
Are you a kid?

154
00:13:08,730 --> 00:13:10,600
One small thing and you have to get even?

155
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,070
Are you picking a fight with me?

156
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:17,700
Why are you two fighting?

157
00:13:22,770 --> 00:13:24,430
Hey, enough!

158
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:28,600
Thanop, I know you've been mad since the last match.

159
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:32,200
But you should settle it, not bottle it up like this.

160
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:35,400
Leaving it hanging like this breaks the team apart.

161
00:13:36,230 --> 00:13:39,670
Aof, same goes for you. You're the team captain.

162
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:43,700
If you let your emotions drive every play like this, how are you going to lead the team, huh?

163
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:45,800
If you don't want the job anymore, tell me.

164
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,270
I'll find someone to replace you.

165
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:51,630
Just say the word. I'll switch you out.

166
00:13:54,470 --> 00:13:56,200
Sorry.

167
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,930
Sorry, Coach.

168
00:14:00,830 --> 00:14:02,370
What do you want?

169
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:03,770
Want to go fight?

170
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:06,130
I'll go sort it out with him myself.

171
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:07,200
Sorry.

172
00:14:09,770 --> 00:14:13,530
Go on, back to practice. Let them fight it out.

173
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:19,670
Thanop.

174
00:14:20,870 --> 00:14:23,070
You're mad at me and you won't say a damn word?

175
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:24,030
Why bottle it up?

176
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:26,030
Who started it?

177
00:14:26,470 --> 00:14:28,400
Tell you every time you act crazy?

178
00:14:29,330 --> 00:14:30,330
We're grown-ups.

179
00:14:30,330 --> 00:14:32,200
So you could've just warned me.

180
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:35,070
Well? We both got chewed out. So embarrassing.

181
00:14:40,470 --> 00:14:43,030
So what's up with you? Tell me.

182
00:14:44,130 --> 00:14:46,400
I'm damn crazy, just like you said.

183
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,470
Come on, punch me once.

184
00:14:48,470 --> 00:14:49,200
Hey!

185
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,800
Might knock my brain back in place.

186
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:53,400
Even if you headbutted the field right now, it wouldn't help.

187
00:14:54,730 --> 00:14:56,630
So are you going to tell me what's wrong?

188
00:14:58,570 --> 00:15:00,030
Well...

189
00:15:00,030 --> 00:15:03,500
So whenever we have practice, I'll message you.

190
00:15:04,130 --> 00:15:06,770
Let's exchange contacts.

191
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:11,270
Oh, sure.

192
00:15:25,230 --> 00:15:26,770
I'm jealous of you and Chemi.

193
00:15:27,930 --> 00:15:29,900
You promised you wouldn't tell anyone.

194
00:15:31,670 --> 00:15:33,270
Okay. I'm holding you to that.

195
00:15:33,270 --> 00:15:34,670
And after this,

196
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:38,430
stay away from Chemi. I don't like it.

197
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:08,130
Hello, testing, testing. 1, 2, 3, 4.

198
00:16:08,130 --> 00:16:11,030
Hello, everyone. I'm Teeraphat Kiattiwong,

199
00:16:11,030 --> 00:16:12,800
representing the student council.

200
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:17,400
Today I have an announcement for everyone about our school event this year.

201
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:19,900
This year, the event has a theme,

202
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:23,270
so we'd love for everyone to share their ideas.

203
00:16:23,270 --> 00:16:27,730
As for planning and any deals, you can come to us for advice anytime.

204
00:16:27,730 --> 00:16:30,930
This year, we plan to make it bigger than ever

205
00:16:30,930 --> 00:16:34,800
by adding stages for music performances and stage plays.

206
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:38,830
Plus more food stalls, shops and game booths.

207
00:16:38,830 --> 00:16:42,530
Most importantly, this year we're offering funding for everyone.

208
00:16:42,530 --> 00:16:45,100
You can contact us at the student council room.

209
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:48,300
But every idea has to be approved first.

210
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:50,900
And don't forget, the event everyone's been waiting for,

211
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:53,900
Thapfah Countdown, is happening as usual.

212
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:57,700
So don't forget to invite that special someone, or the one you've got your eye on,

213
00:16:57,700 --> 00:16:59,230
well in advance.

214
00:16:59,230 --> 00:17:01,330
That's all for the announcement.

215
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:03,930
From the student council, thank you.

216
00:17:18,369 --> 00:17:21,329
I think we should put the game booths here.

217
00:17:21,329 --> 00:17:24,300
And the handmade stuff can go under the building.

218
00:17:25,030 --> 00:17:27,500
Take it from here, Chok. That's all I prepared.

219
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:32,770
Supplies too, Nam.

220
00:17:33,570 --> 00:17:34,800
As for the orange courtyard,

221
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:37,100
we'll use it for music in the first round.

222
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,800
Then after the party's over,

223
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:41,400
we'll switch back to the stage we use for the plays.

224
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:43,530
What do you think, Din?

225
00:17:44,470 --> 00:17:45,970
Mm, I'm good with it.

226
00:17:47,570 --> 00:17:48,970
As for ticket sales,

227
00:17:48,970 --> 00:17:51,900
I think we open a presale round first, then go back to the regular price.

228
00:17:52,430 --> 00:17:55,230
And keep some to sell on the day. / Sure.

229
00:17:55,930 --> 00:17:58,070
I'll go deal with the booths. / Mm.

230
00:17:58,070 --> 00:18:00,570
And that Kim kid you asked us to find,

231
00:18:00,570 --> 00:18:02,170
we found him.

232
00:18:02,170 --> 00:18:04,270
Whoa, what did he say? Is he in?

233
00:18:04,270 --> 00:18:06,200
Of course. Who'd say no to us?

234
00:18:07,570 --> 00:18:09,400
But he doesn't talk much.

235
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:11,500
He just said he wants to pick the cast himself.

236
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,230
Doesn't sound like a problem.

237
00:18:13,230 --> 00:18:14,630
Mm, I guess so.

238
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:20,500
Mr. Din, has your first mission come in yet?

239
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:22,330
Well, Din?

240
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,470
Guess they don't want me to do it anymore.

241
00:18:25,470 --> 00:18:28,800
Aw, somebody's sulking.

242
00:18:38,430 --> 00:18:39,730
Whoa, what's this?

243
00:18:40,630 --> 00:18:41,600
Din!

244
00:18:46,230 --> 00:18:49,530
Did the first mission come in? Is it hard?

245
00:18:52,130 --> 00:18:54,530
Look at him smiling. / Is it hard?

246
00:18:58,830 --> 00:19:00,030
Easier than you'd think.

247
00:19:00,030 --> 00:19:02,070
"Mission 1: Take Star to his tutoring class"

248
00:19:02,070 --> 00:19:03,430
Nice one, Din.

249
00:19:03,430 --> 00:19:05,130
Real big-league stuff.

250
00:19:12,370 --> 00:19:13,570
What's your name?

251
00:19:15,770 --> 00:19:17,070
Din.

252
00:19:19,030 --> 00:19:21,630
What grade are you in? And which track?

253
00:19:23,730 --> 00:19:26,430
M.6, science and math track.

254
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:30,130
You're also the student president, right?

255
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:32,870
Studying and working at the same time,

256
00:19:32,870 --> 00:19:34,730
how do you manage it all?

257
00:19:35,630 --> 00:19:38,800
Honestly, being president isn't that much work,

258
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,270
because my friends help out.

259
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:42,870
And for school, I just split my time as usual.

260
00:19:42,870 --> 00:19:44,470
I don't have to miss any classes, sir.

261
00:19:53,630 --> 00:19:55,000
Din...

262
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:59,370
Thank you so much for saving Star.

263
00:20:01,370 --> 00:20:02,470
Of course.

264
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:07,830
So how long have you two been together?

265
00:20:08,630 --> 00:20:11,200
Dad! Together? What are you talking about?

266
00:20:11,970 --> 00:20:14,930
Well, you brought him home to meet me.

267
00:20:14,930 --> 00:20:16,830
Don't jump to conclusions, Dad.

268
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,030
Okay, okay. Let's change the subject.

269
00:20:20,830 --> 00:20:23,600
Let's go, Samai.

270
00:20:28,930 --> 00:20:30,430
Are you seeing anyone, Din?

271
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:33,430
Dad! Don't ask him that too!

272
00:20:33,430 --> 00:20:38,800
What? I want to know. So, Din? Are you seeing anyone?

273
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:42,570
Not right now.

274
00:20:45,100 --> 00:20:47,000
Hard to believe

275
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,500
a guy like you is still available.

276
00:20:51,870 --> 00:20:56,770
If you ask me, whoever gets to date you and lets you slip away

277
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:59,000
would really regret it.

278
00:21:00,130 --> 00:21:01,400
Dad...

279
00:21:19,130 --> 00:21:20,070
You drive.

280
00:21:20,730 --> 00:21:22,000
Why are you making me drive?

281
00:21:22,330 --> 00:21:25,400
Well, you always complain that I never let you drive.

282
00:21:27,330 --> 00:21:29,400
What are you planning? Trying to kill me?

283
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:31,200
What? No plan.

284
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:32,600
I'm just letting you drive.

285
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:36,570
Okay, okay. / I'm starving.

286
00:21:36,570 --> 00:21:38,370
I want some of your dad's cooking.

287
00:21:46,670 --> 00:21:48,430
You know how to wear a helmet, right?

288
00:21:48,930 --> 00:21:50,030
Yeah.

289
00:21:56,770 --> 00:21:58,930
Ready? / Not yet.

290
00:21:58,930 --> 00:22:01,070
Are you sure you can drive this?

291
00:22:01,070 --> 00:22:02,170
Sure.

292
00:22:04,670 --> 00:22:05,730
Wait, wait, wait.

293
00:22:06,130 --> 00:22:07,200
Spread your arms first.

294
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,200
Why?

295
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:11,600
Hold still. Don't put your arms down.

296
00:22:26,870 --> 00:22:28,030
Okay.

297
00:22:29,830 --> 00:22:31,200
What are you playing at?

298
00:22:31,530 --> 00:22:32,630
Playing?

299
00:22:33,930 --> 00:22:35,500
I'm not playing. I'm serious.

300
00:22:35,870 --> 00:22:38,130
I don't know how good a driver you are.

301
00:22:38,930 --> 00:22:41,400
Ah, okay. Fine.

302
00:22:49,430 --> 00:22:51,200
Ready? / Yeah.

303
00:23:01,030 --> 00:23:06,300
♪ Beside you every day, but I have to act like I don't care ♪

304
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:11,570
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it inside ♪

305
00:23:11,570 --> 00:23:17,500
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

306
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:22,770
♪ I know what's between us should stay unsaid ♪

307
00:23:30,500 --> 00:23:32,700
So how are you getting home this evening?

308
00:23:33,270 --> 00:23:35,330
I'll just call a car.

309
00:23:35,330 --> 00:23:37,270
That way you can go back with Samai.

310
00:23:37,870 --> 00:23:39,330
Are you sure?

311
00:23:40,270 --> 00:23:41,800
Don't worry.

312
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:44,370
I'll ride with Star to keep him company.

313
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,970
Then please look after Star.

314
00:23:49,730 --> 00:23:51,070
Yes, sir.

315
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:16,700
Samai, you can go wait in the car. Thank you.

316
00:24:25,330 --> 00:24:27,030
Oh, Din.

317
00:24:30,300 --> 00:24:33,130
You really don't have to go this far.

318
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:36,270
Just pass the mission and I'll give you the first ID.

319
00:24:37,230 --> 00:24:39,600
Well, I could see your dad was worried.

320
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:41,200
Plus, our places aren't far apart.

321
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:42,330
It's no trouble.

322
00:24:44,730 --> 00:24:47,600
Are you always this nice to everyone?

323
00:24:58,470 --> 00:25:01,070
You could tone down the niceness a bit, Din.

324
00:25:12,570 --> 00:25:16,000
Or everyone will think you're hitting on them.

325
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:18,530
Mm. Thanks for the warning.

326
00:25:18,530 --> 00:25:21,970
Uh, if you think anything's too much, just tell me.

327
00:25:22,370 --> 00:25:26,600
Do you realize you're actually really stubborn, Din?

328
00:25:27,370 --> 00:25:29,870
No matter what, you'll get it done.

329
00:25:30,330 --> 00:25:32,100
But promise me,

330
00:25:32,530 --> 00:25:35,200
if there's ever a day you can't take it, you have to stop.

331
00:25:42,030 --> 00:25:42,930
I promise.

332
00:25:43,500 --> 00:25:45,800
If I ever can't take it, I'll stop myself.

333
00:25:50,170 --> 00:25:52,830
Then I'm heading to class.

334
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,230
Honey, hurry up. The kids are hungry.

335
00:26:20,230 --> 00:26:21,370
Okay, okay. Hungry already?

336
00:26:21,370 --> 00:26:23,030
Wipe there too, sweetie. / Come on.

337
00:26:25,470 --> 00:26:27,730
Hey. / Hm?

338
00:26:27,730 --> 00:26:31,700
Is your dad still going out to supervise the sites himself?

339
00:26:31,700 --> 00:26:35,030
Or is this project so big he has to go supervise again?

340
00:26:35,530 --> 00:26:39,130
Big or small, he supervises every job himself.

341
00:26:39,700 --> 00:26:42,400
And that's after he's trained the company guys well.

342
00:26:42,930 --> 00:26:46,630
At first they were tense, thinking Dad didn't trust them.

343
00:26:46,630 --> 00:26:49,630
Now they all get that he just loves to work.

344
00:26:51,130 --> 00:26:55,230
Now it's kind of like his own little family.

345
00:26:56,830 --> 00:27:01,770
Mom and I see how happy he is with work, so we understand him.

346
00:27:06,830 --> 00:27:09,130
Doesn't your mom get lonely like this?

347
00:27:10,900 --> 00:27:12,670
I used to think so too.

348
00:27:13,330 --> 00:27:16,170
But... Mom seems fine.

349
00:27:16,900 --> 00:27:18,670
Maybe she's like your mom.

350
00:27:20,800 --> 00:27:23,470
Hmm, when you think about it...

351
00:27:24,470 --> 00:27:26,570
our families are kind of alike.

352
00:27:26,570 --> 00:27:27,700
True.

353
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:38,500
Food's here! Are you kids hungry?

354
00:27:39,370 --> 00:27:41,270
Sure am!

355
00:27:42,100 --> 00:27:45,130
Your favorite. Mom made it herself.

356
00:27:45,130 --> 00:27:49,070
Sweetie, this clear soup is good for you.

357
00:27:49,530 --> 00:27:51,670
Yes. Whoa, crispy pork.

358
00:27:51,670 --> 00:27:52,770
That's right.

359
00:27:52,770 --> 00:27:54,230
This is Mom's cooking, you know.

360
00:27:54,230 --> 00:27:56,030
You bet! / Good boy.

361
00:27:57,900 --> 00:27:59,000
How've you been, Physics?

362
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,600
Haven't seen you in ages.

363
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:01,630
Doing well?

364
00:28:02,730 --> 00:28:05,500
Yes, I've been well.

365
00:28:05,500 --> 00:28:09,130
Well, you hardly ever come home. How would you see him?

366
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:12,300
Mm, fair enough. But next year,

367
00:28:12,300 --> 00:28:14,370
I'm planning to spend less time on site.

368
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:17,400
Mean it this time, Dad.

369
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:21,400
Give it two or three days and you'll find an excuse to go again.

370
00:28:22,370 --> 00:28:24,330
Believe me just this once, son.

371
00:28:24,330 --> 00:28:27,030
Over there, they can manage.

372
00:28:27,030 --> 00:28:31,270
But when I have to work far from your mom for a long time,

373
00:28:31,930 --> 00:28:34,370
I miss her like crazy.

374
00:28:40,130 --> 00:28:42,130
You miss me too, right?

375
00:28:44,670 --> 00:28:47,330
Isn't that a bit too sweet? / Hm?

376
00:28:49,330 --> 00:28:51,930
Cheeky. They're my parents, you know.

377
00:28:57,430 --> 00:29:02,270
You two are so close. Don't ever break up.

378
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:04,930
Physics.

379
00:29:06,100 --> 00:29:07,170
Yes?

380
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:09,870
Dad, why so serious?

381
00:29:17,970 --> 00:29:20,030
I won't ask for much of a dowry.

382
00:29:20,330 --> 00:29:21,700
Go tell your parents.

383
00:29:22,030 --> 00:29:22,970
Dad!

384
00:29:25,700 --> 00:29:27,500
Who else could put up with you?

385
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:29,130
You're the most spoiled one around.

386
00:29:29,130 --> 00:29:33,000
With Physics around, your mom and I can rest in peace.

387
00:29:33,970 --> 00:29:37,570
Trust me. Handsome, rich, and so good at pampering you,

388
00:29:37,570 --> 00:29:39,270
you'll be set for life.

389
00:29:41,770 --> 00:29:43,330
I'm not bad, sir.

390
00:29:43,630 --> 00:29:45,170
Oh, so you're accepting, huh?

391
00:29:45,170 --> 00:29:48,200
Well, your dad set it up like that, so I have to take it.

392
00:29:49,670 --> 00:29:54,970
But first, let me win Fuen over.

393
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:57,930
Of course.

394
00:29:58,430 --> 00:30:00,500
Fuen, don't play too hard to get.

395
00:30:00,500 --> 00:30:02,430
Mom, you're on their side too?

396
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:08,730
Listen to your mom for once. Don't play hard to get.

397
00:30:09,100 --> 00:30:10,330
Just shut up and eat.

398
00:30:10,830 --> 00:30:12,600
You mean your mom and me?

399
00:30:12,800 --> 00:30:14,770
Oops, no, no, no. Not you, Dad. Not you, Mom.

400
00:30:15,430 --> 00:30:16,630
My heart skipped a beat.

401
00:30:16,630 --> 00:30:18,970
Let's just eat. / Okay, let's eat.

402
00:30:18,970 --> 00:30:20,970
Here, try some pork sausage.

403
00:30:21,870 --> 00:30:24,170
Say ahh...

404
00:30:25,330 --> 00:30:27,400
Delicious.

405
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:53,770
Wow, it's so cool today.

406
00:30:59,870 --> 00:31:01,270
So refreshing.

407
00:31:05,570 --> 00:31:06,570
Chemi.

408
00:31:08,470 --> 00:31:10,470
Come sit and talk with me.

409
00:31:36,630 --> 00:31:41,830
Do you remember what you told me when I was little?

410
00:31:47,970 --> 00:31:50,570
How about this — if you don't have anyone by then,

411
00:31:50,570 --> 00:31:52,470
I'll be your first boyfriend myself.

412
00:31:58,970 --> 00:32:01,200
Deal.

413
00:32:06,430 --> 00:32:09,230
Back then, I believed every word with all my heart.

414
00:32:12,200 --> 00:32:15,670
I thought you'd definitely keep your word.

415
00:32:16,770 --> 00:32:24,570
I thought you were the most sincere person I knew, the one who kept his promises.

416
00:32:34,300 --> 00:32:36,400
I really want to know...

417
00:32:38,530 --> 00:32:42,330
if you really like me, or just came to collect on the promise from when you were a kid.

418
00:32:57,900 --> 00:33:01,830
At first I thought we felt the same way.

419
00:33:05,170 --> 00:33:07,000
But now I don't know.

420
00:33:11,430 --> 00:33:13,630
I want to keep my promise too.

421
00:33:16,570 --> 00:33:18,400
But...

422
00:33:22,530 --> 00:33:24,730
there's something I have to take care of first.

423
00:33:24,730 --> 00:33:25,970
What is it?

424
00:33:28,670 --> 00:33:31,730
Had a lot of fun going out with my brother?

425
00:33:33,930 --> 00:33:35,470
So when are you going to stop?

426
00:33:35,470 --> 00:33:36,770
Stop what?

427
00:33:36,770 --> 00:33:38,300
Stop messing with my brother.

428
00:33:39,300 --> 00:33:40,730
Don't think I don't know.

429
00:33:41,770 --> 00:33:44,100
It's something about me.

430
00:33:49,770 --> 00:33:53,070
Right now I'm totally confused.

431
00:33:58,370 --> 00:34:01,130
Then why don't we just forget about back then?

432
00:34:02,370 --> 00:34:08,070
It was just something kids said anyway.

433
00:34:10,670 --> 00:34:12,000
Chemi.

434
00:34:17,870 --> 00:34:19,969
I mean it, Aof.

435
00:34:26,929 --> 00:34:28,969
Back then, you told me to grow up first.

436
00:34:30,230 --> 00:34:32,270
So I waited until I was grown up enough.

437
00:34:35,100 --> 00:34:37,969
When I asked you and you didn't answer,

438
00:34:39,730 --> 00:34:41,900
I still waited for you.

439
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:53,270
And to this day... you haven't done a single thing you said you would.

440
00:34:59,070 --> 00:35:01,800
I don't know what I'm waiting for either.

441
00:35:20,030 --> 00:35:21,730
You don't have to answer.

442
00:35:25,830 --> 00:35:30,100
I think your silence is answer enough.

443
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:45,300
I'm going to go.

444
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:57,870
♪ I want to ask you once more, do you still remember ♪

445
00:35:57,870 --> 00:36:02,930
♪ what you told me back then ♪

446
00:36:02,930 --> 00:36:08,000
♪ Or am I the only one who hasn't moved on ♪

447
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:13,930
♪ The questions in my heart, I have to keep inside ♪

448
00:36:13,930 --> 00:36:18,400
♪ Today, if you still feel the same ♪

449
00:36:18,400 --> 00:36:23,500
♪ don't let that day be our last ♪

450
00:36:23,500 --> 00:36:29,530
♪ the memories we share, the nights and days ♪

451
00:36:29,530 --> 00:36:33,900
♪ that place, is it still there ♪

452
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:38,870
♪ Every day goes by, it never fades ♪

453
00:36:38,870 --> 00:36:47,430
♪ The feelings back then, the story back then, I still remember ♪

454
00:36:47,430 --> 00:36:57,230
♪ The smile you gave me, that day we sat side by side ♪

455
00:36:57,230 --> 00:37:08,130
♪ We once made a promise that we'd have each other ♪

456
00:37:57,700 --> 00:38:00,600
Din, have you been waiting long?

457
00:38:01,270 --> 00:38:02,630
Let's go eat.

458
00:38:02,630 --> 00:38:03,600
Star.

459
00:38:05,830 --> 00:38:06,630
Oh!

460
00:38:07,100 --> 00:38:08,770
Rei, what are you doing here?

461
00:38:13,530 --> 00:38:14,770
I came to call in a promise.

462
00:38:14,770 --> 00:38:15,970
Let's go eat.

463
00:38:27,730 --> 00:38:30,030
Then let's all go eat together.

464
00:38:43,670 --> 00:38:45,930
What did you want to talk to me about, Rei?

465
00:38:45,930 --> 00:38:48,270
I wanted to apologize about the busking day.

466
00:38:48,730 --> 00:38:50,630
I really didn't mean to not show up.

467
00:38:50,630 --> 00:38:52,600
It's okay, Rei. I understand.

468
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:54,300
Besides, that was a long time ago.

469
00:38:54,300 --> 00:38:55,530
You're not mad at me, right?

470
00:38:56,600 --> 00:38:57,970
I'm not mad, Rei.

471
00:39:02,470 --> 00:39:04,070
Thank you.

472
00:39:04,500 --> 00:39:06,870
I ordered things I thought you'd like, Star.

473
00:39:10,170 --> 00:39:11,630
Thank you, Din.

474
00:39:49,930 --> 00:39:51,670
I don't want to rush into dating.

475
00:39:53,070 --> 00:39:54,670
That's totally fine.

476
00:39:55,600 --> 00:39:57,030
You don't have to rush at all.

477
00:39:57,400 --> 00:39:58,830
Mom? / Hm?

478
00:40:01,170 --> 00:40:04,900
Why is it so hard to have a boyfriend?

479
00:40:12,770 --> 00:40:16,470
Maybe it's hard because we make it hard ourselves.

480
00:40:19,470 --> 00:40:23,170
And when you and Dad started dating, wasn't it hard?

481
00:40:24,670 --> 00:40:30,170
No, because I asked your dad straight out whether we'd keep going or stop there.

482
00:40:31,030 --> 00:40:33,000
If he liked me... we'd keep going.

483
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:36,170
If not... we'd stop right there.

484
00:40:37,530 --> 00:40:39,370
And after that,

485
00:40:40,300 --> 00:40:42,330
your dad asked me to be his girlfriend.

486
00:40:45,430 --> 00:40:46,430
Yes, dear.

487
00:40:53,070 --> 00:41:00,370
And what if back then you'd asked Dad, but he didn't answer?

488
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:02,900
Would you still have kept going?

489
00:41:04,730 --> 00:41:05,630
No.

490
00:41:06,300 --> 00:41:08,670
Stop. I would've stopped right there.

491
00:41:10,070 --> 00:41:12,630
Because not being clear is an answer in itself, sweetie.

492
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:16,630
If he wants you in his life,

493
00:41:17,970 --> 00:41:19,500
he'll do everything

494
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:21,600
to keep you.

495
00:41:37,100 --> 00:41:38,670
I love you, Mom.

496
00:41:40,730 --> 00:41:42,930
I love you too, sweetie.

497
00:41:43,470 --> 00:41:45,200
My little boy.

498
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:50,500
I'm going to sleep. / Oh?

499
00:41:50,500 --> 00:41:51,500
Right here.

500
00:41:51,500 --> 00:41:52,500
Right here? / Yeah.

501
00:41:52,500 --> 00:41:55,870
Without brushing your teeth? / It's fine, I'll brush tomorrow.

502
00:41:56,800 --> 00:41:59,400
Not even taking off your glasses? Here, let me.

503
00:42:02,700 --> 00:42:03,570
Thanks.

504
00:42:32,370 --> 00:42:33,330
Ugh.

505
00:42:34,530 --> 00:42:36,700
So why didn't you just give him a proper answer?

506
00:42:40,270 --> 00:42:43,930
Ugh... Yell at me all you want, but help me out.

507
00:42:47,600 --> 00:42:49,670
Go talk to Physics straight.

508
00:42:49,670 --> 00:42:51,670
And then explain it to Chemi too.

509
00:42:52,970 --> 00:42:54,900
And explain what, exactly?

510
00:42:54,900 --> 00:42:58,830
Explain that I really like Chemi,

511
00:42:58,830 --> 00:43:01,830
but I'm holding back out of respect for Physics?

512
00:43:03,330 --> 00:43:04,500
Ugh.

513
00:43:05,030 --> 00:43:07,100
Who's the 12-year-old here, you or him?

514
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:10,230
Chemi may be younger than you,

515
00:43:10,230 --> 00:43:12,830
but he's still more grown-up than you, you idiot.

516
00:43:15,830 --> 00:43:17,470
Didn't he say it himself?

517
00:43:17,470 --> 00:43:20,200
To forget about back then and start over.

518
00:43:20,930 --> 00:43:22,300
But you didn't answer.

519
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:25,870
What the hell's stuck in your mouth, huh?

520
00:43:29,130 --> 00:43:31,130
Words matter. That's why I didn't dare.

521
00:43:32,530 --> 00:43:33,800
Last time,

522
00:43:34,470 --> 00:43:37,500
I spoke without thinking once, and I hurt him.

523
00:43:37,500 --> 00:43:39,300
And what if I do it again this time?

524
00:43:41,730 --> 00:43:43,500
You single-brain-cell animal!

525
00:43:44,470 --> 00:43:45,770
Let me hit you just once!

526
00:43:45,770 --> 00:43:48,300
If I were Chemi, there's no way I'd take you.

527
00:43:50,030 --> 00:43:52,700
If you can't say it, why not write it?

528
00:43:53,870 --> 00:43:57,470
When my dad messes up and wants to explain things to my mom,

529
00:43:57,470 --> 00:43:59,430
he writes it all down.

530
00:43:59,930 --> 00:44:01,630
The end. Happy ending.

531
00:44:02,300 --> 00:44:04,630
Damn! Why didn't I think of that?

532
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:08,870
Then I'm copying your dad. Hold on, be right back.

533
00:44:13,870 --> 00:44:15,800
No wonder they call you Aof.

534
00:44:16,570 --> 00:44:19,430
Single-brain-cell idiot. Fine, I'll play by myself.

535
00:44:47,170 --> 00:44:50,330
You should go home. Have you called a car?

536
00:44:58,870 --> 00:45:00,100
I'm not going home.

537
00:45:04,700 --> 00:45:06,300
This is my house.

538
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:10,570
Your dad already said it's okay.

539
00:45:17,170 --> 00:45:18,600
School uniform.

540
00:45:20,830 --> 00:45:23,230
How can you stay over? You've got no uniform.

541
00:45:25,600 --> 00:45:29,270
Right here. School uniform.

542
00:45:31,030 --> 00:45:32,600
Just go home, you slob.

543
00:45:33,730 --> 00:45:35,300
I want to sleep alone tonight.

544
00:45:37,130 --> 00:45:39,100
Fine.

545
00:45:53,300 --> 00:45:55,000
What's with you, Physics?

546
00:45:56,370 --> 00:45:58,000
Just go home.

547
00:46:03,300 --> 00:46:04,700
Go home? How am I supposed to?

548
00:46:24,200 --> 00:46:25,470
What are you thinking?

549
00:46:29,930 --> 00:46:31,270
Thinking something crazy?

550
00:46:31,670 --> 00:46:33,370
I'm not thinking anything. / Good.

551
00:46:34,600 --> 00:46:36,170
If you're not thinking anything,

552
00:46:36,170 --> 00:46:38,830
then we're still just normal friends.

553
00:46:39,970 --> 00:46:41,470
So we can share a bed.

554
00:46:42,830 --> 00:46:45,970
Hey, that's not it, Physics.

555
00:47:34,070 --> 00:47:37,030
Aren't you going to sleep? You keep fidgeting.

556
00:47:39,600 --> 00:47:41,100
Mind your own business.

557
00:47:41,100 --> 00:47:42,500
Just go to sleep.

558
00:48:08,330 --> 00:48:09,530
Physics.

559
00:48:17,970 --> 00:48:20,000
There's something I want to tell you.

560
00:48:21,200 --> 00:48:23,470
You don't have to be afraid of me.

561
00:48:25,030 --> 00:48:26,930
You can definitely trust me.

562
00:48:32,170 --> 00:48:35,430
I can always wait for you.

563
00:49:00,030 --> 00:49:02,670
But don't get too carried away with me.

564
00:49:03,600 --> 00:49:06,230
Physics, you're going too far. Hey!

565
00:49:06,570 --> 00:49:09,530
You're messing with me way too much. / Aren't you going to sleep?

566
00:49:25,630 --> 00:49:26,970
Didn't you say you could fool me?

567
00:49:28,870 --> 00:49:30,930
What? You wanna fight?

568
00:49:33,730 --> 00:49:37,930
Come on, come on, come on. / Get off my bed.

569
00:50:41,230 --> 00:50:44,800
"Soulmate or Best friend? I'm waiting for your answer."

570
00:50:44,800 --> 00:50:48,600
There's something I want to tell you. You don't have to be afraid of me.

571
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:52,200
You can definitely trust me.

572
00:50:52,200 --> 00:50:55,000
I can always wait for you.

573
00:50:55,000 --> 00:51:05,400
♪ I slip and give you my heart, I slip and watch you every day, my heart can't take it ♪

574
00:51:05,400 --> 00:51:11,270
♪ Beside you every day, but I have to act like I don't care ♪

575
00:51:11,270 --> 00:51:16,300
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it inside ♪

576
00:51:16,300 --> 00:51:21,700
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

577
00:51:21,700 --> 00:51:27,330
♪ I know what's between us should stay unsaid ♪

578
00:51:41,600 --> 00:51:46,330
"Really? So how long have you two been together? Well, you brought him home to meet me."

579
00:51:47,000 --> 00:51:50,070
"If there's ever a day I can't take it, I'll give up on my own. (Din)"

580
00:51:50,070 --> 00:51:52,430
"It's a promise, then. (Star)"

581
00:51:52,630 --> 00:51:54,100
"Maybe it's not your fault, Aof..."

582
00:51:54,100 --> 00:51:55,970
"Maybe I took what you said too seriously."

583
00:51:55,970 --> 00:51:58,100
"Anyone can say 'I'll ask you out when you grow up.'"

584
00:51:59,370 --> 00:52:03,070
Chemi, could you take this, please? I spent all night writing it.

585
00:52:03,070 --> 00:52:04,730
I want you to read it.

586
00:52:04,730 --> 00:52:05,770
You want me to do what?

587
00:52:05,770 --> 00:52:06,870
Be in the stage play.

588
00:52:06,870 --> 00:52:08,070
Do you hate it that much?

589
00:52:08,970 --> 00:52:10,370
There's a kiss scene.

590
00:52:10,370 --> 00:52:11,600
What! Seriously?

591
00:52:11,600 --> 00:52:14,530
I think you should stop doing the missions, Din.

592
00:52:14,530 --> 00:52:18,270
Why? Are you upset with me about something, Star?

593
00:52:18,270 --> 00:52:20,970
Star, let me take you home.

594
00:52:20,970 --> 00:52:22,830
Oh, Si, did you buy this for me?

595
00:52:22,830 --> 00:52:23,770
I didn't buy it.

596
00:52:23,770 --> 00:52:25,330
Then whose is this?
